"In the movie \"Mean Girls 2: The Sequel,\" at a high school dance.\n\nSCENE: Cady, the main character, is dancing with her friend Troy. Suddenly, she spots a group of popular girls dancing together, and one of them, Gretchen Wieners, catches her eye.\n\nCady (in a sarcastic tone, whispering to Troy): \"Isn't that Gretchen? The one with the dumb blonde hair... and the dumb blonde attitude.\"\n\nTroy (confused): \"Cady, is that how you want to sound?\"\n\nCady (rolling her eyes): \"Oh, come on, Troy. We need to get her back for all the jokes they've made about us.\"\n\nGretchen (overhearing): \"What did you say, Cady? You think you're so clever, huh? Well, let me tell you something, blonde girl... you don't even know the meaning of the word 'dumb.'\"\n\nCady (playfully): \"Oh, here we go again. I can't wait to see what ridiculous excuse you'll come up with next.\"\n\nTroy (trying to diffuse the situation): \"Cady, maybe we should just dance and have fun.\"\n\nCady (smirking): \"Yeah, but it's more fun to watch them squirm, isn't it?\"\n\nGretchen (mocking Cady's accent): \"Well, you better watch out, Cady. You might just end up being the dumb blonde if you keep talking like that.\"\n\nCady (teasingly): \"Oh, don't worry, Gretchen. I'll just keep being me, and you'll keep being you... a total ditz.\"\n\nTroy (whispering): \"Should we tell her off or just walk away?\"\n\nCady (deciding): \"Let's just enjoy the moment. I've been waiting for this for too long.\"\n\nTroy (smiling): \"Alright, but remember, Cady. We're not like them.\"\n\nCady (nodding): \"I know, Troy. And I'm proud of who I am.\"\n\nTroy (grinning): \"Good, because we're going to have a lot more fun if we stay true to ourselves.\"\n\nCady (laughing): \"Let's go show them who we really are!\""
